     A                                      ------------------------------------
     A                                      ---------'
     A                                  4  2': The first screen allows the craf-
     A                                      tsman to select from the reserved w-
     A                                      orkorder:'
     A                                  5  2': list, those workorders which he -
     A                                      has completed   those on which he h-
     A                                      as      :'
     A                                  6  2': performed labor but has not comp-
     A                                      leted   and any which he may have r-
     A                                      eserved :'
     A                                  7  2': but did not perform any labor.  -
     A                                      The first workorder is always that -
     A                                      which he:'
     A                                  8  2': is signed "IP" onto.  Enter a "0-
     A                                      ", "1" or "2" as instructed from th-
     A                                      e screen:'
     A                                  9  2': and press the "ENTER" key.  The -
     A                                      "f1" thru "f6" keys will display th-
     A                                      e       :'
     A                                 10  2': corresponding workorder if desir-
     A                                      ed.                                -
     A                                              :'
     A                                 11  2'1----------------------------------
     A                                      ------------------------------------
     A                                      ---------'
     A                                 12  2': The second screen allows the tot-
     A                                      al labor time to be apportioned amo-
     A                                      ng the  :'
     A                                 13  2': various reserved workorders.  Th-
     A                                      e total number of labor minutes fro-
     A                                      m the   :'
     A                                 14  2': initial "IP" time to the current-
     A                                       clock time are given.  Enter the l-
     A                                      abor    :'
     A                                 15  2': minutes spent on each workorder -
     A                                      and press the "ENTER" key to calcul-
     A                                      ate the :'
     A                                 16  2': proper start and stop times.  An-
     A                                      y labor minutes may be changed and -
     A                                      the     :'
     A                                 17  2': "ENTER" key may be pressed as of-
     A                                      ten as desired to allow the program-
     A                                       to     :'
     A                                 18  2': re-calculate the times until the-
     A                                       craftsman is satisfied that the nu-
     A                                      mbers   :'
     A                                 19  2': are correct.  When a labor time -
     A                                      has been entered for each workorder-
     A                                       on the :'
     A                                 20  2': list, and when the labor minutes-
     A                                       left unaccounted for is equal to z-
     A                                      ero,    :'
     A                                 21  2': press the "f5" key to write the -
     A                                      labor records.                     -
     A                                              :'
